{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\n`_metered_spend()` in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` accumulated token spend across regions, but a single CloudWatch `ClientError` discarded totals already collected from healthy regions and returned `None`.\n\n## Design\n\nReturn a frozen `MeteredSpend(total, degraded, failures)` where each `MeteredFailure` records the failed region and exception class. If at least 1 token series contributes, return a degraded `MeteredSpend` carrying the partial total; if a `ClientError` prevents a complete scan before any series contributes, keep the unavailable path and return `None`.\n\nSequenced after `604c-ade8`, which removed the unconditional `metered is None` CE-poll trigger so a metered outage cannot override `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`. This change must not reintroduce that trigger, nor add a `metered.degraded` equivalent. `MeteredSpend.total` is a lower bound, so the near-threshold test can be false while full regional spend would be true; that is handled by carrying `degraded=True` into release safety and operator visibility rather than by polling more often.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` defines `MeteredSpend`.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.total` stores the numeric CloudWatch dollar total.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True` when at least 1 region raises `ClientError` during the scan.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed region name.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed exception class.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `list_metrics`.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `get_metric_data`.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` continues scanning later regions after an earlier region raises `ClientError`.\n- [x] When a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan before any token series contributes, `_metered_spend()` returns `None`.\n- [x] Degraded-region logging includes the failed region name.\n- [x] Degraded-region logging includes the exception class name.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate uses `MeteredSpend.total` for near-threshold arithmetic.\n- [x] A degraded partial below the near-threshold amount does not poll CE before the due interval.\n- [x] A degraded partial at the near-threshold amount polls CE before the due interval.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered.degraded` trigger.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered is None` trigger reintroduced by cfe0.\n- [x] `signal_unavailable` is `True` when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total >= THRESHOLD_USD` attaches the deny policy when it is not attached.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` leaves an existing deny policy attached.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` publishes no release notification.\n- [x] Metered log text reports the numeric partial total when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` extends `FakeAWS.client()` so CloudWatch fakes can vary by `region_name`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_listing_fails` covers the listing-failure partial.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_data_fails` covers the data-failure partial.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers region name logging.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers exception class logging.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_below_near_threshold_respects_ce_interval` covers the non-due no-poll case.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_at_near_threshold_polls_ce` covers the near-threshold poll case.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_can_attach` covers fail-closed attachment.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_cannot_release` covers release blocking.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_cloudwatch_failure_before_any_series_reports_unavailable` covers the `None` fallback.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` exits 0.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nVerified against merged commit `1f338f2c57e` (Gerrit change 2997, tip of `origin/main`) in a throwaway detached worktree.\n\n- `MeteredSpend` at `handler.py:288` with `total` (289), `failures` (291); `MeteredFailure.exception_class` at 284.\n- Degraded construction at `handler.py:371`; the `None` pre-contribution path at `367-368`.\n- Both failure paths log then `continue` (`344-346` listing, `357-359` data), so later regions are still scanned; degraded logging carries region and exception class at `301-303`.\n- CE-poll gate is `if due or near_threshold:` at `handler.py:535`, `near_threshold` derived from `metered.total` at `533-534`. No bare `metered.degraded` and no bare `metered is None` disjunct, so 604c's removal stands.\n- `signal_unavailable` includes `metered.degraded` at `565-568`; attach at `621-623`; release requires `not signal_unavailable` at `608`; numeric partial logged at `570` and `578`.\n- `FakeAWS.client()` varies CloudWatch by `region_name` at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:169-186`; all 9 named tests exist and assert the claimed behaviour, at lines 432, 472, 515, 697, 719, 773, 790 and 1389.\n- `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` -> `61 passed in 16.26s`.\n- `make verify` passed in CI: change 2997 carried `Verified +1`, which runs the gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell `make verify` mirrors."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789891024324452824,"uuid":"791185d3-a335-4d68-aa4a-7b1adca1fddd"}